              "question": "<p class=\"Normal ParaOverride-63\" lang=\"en-US\" xml:lang=\"en-US\">Let&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(E_{n} = \\frac{- 1m e^{4}}{8 \\varepsilon_{0}^{2}n^{2} h^{2}} \\)</span>&nbsp;be the energy of the <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(n^\\text{th}\\)</span> level of H-atom. If all the H-atoms are in the ground state and radiation of frequency&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{\\left(\\right. E_{2} - E_{1} \\left.\\right)}{h}\\)</span>&nbsp;falls on it, then:</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"min-width: 300px;\"><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td>it will not be absorbed at all.</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td>some of the atoms will move to the first excited state.</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td>all atoms will be excited to the <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(n = 2\\)</span> state.</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td>no atoms will make a transition to the <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(n = 3\\)</span> state.</td></tr></tbody></table>Choose the correct option:<br>&nbsp;\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"min-width: 300px;\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>(b, d)</td><td>2.</td><td>(a, d)</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>(b, c, d)</td><td>4.</td><td>(c, d)</td></tr></tbody></table>",
